/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Take the root at x = 0 and the tip at x = L.
   - V is the shear force in N at station x; w is the net load per unit span in N/m, positive upward; x is distance from the root in m; L is the semi-span in m; ξ is a dummy span coordinate in m.
   - M is the bending moment in N·m at station x; V, w, x, L and ξ are as above.
   - The part of the wing outboard of x carries all the net load beyond x.
   - For a uniform net load w, V = w(L − x) and M = w(L − x)²/2.
   - An engine, a store or a landing gear adds a downward point load: the shear jumps there and the moment changes slope, as worked example 2 shows.
   - Real lift is not uniform along the span: it depends on planform, twist and the trailing vortices.
   - An elliptic lift distribution has minimum induced drag for a given span and a given total lift.
   - wlift is the estimated lift per unit span in N/m; well is the elliptic distribution in N/m; wplan is the planform distribution in N/m, proportional to chord c(x); the constant of proportionality is chosen so the total lift equals the requir
   - Taper moves load inboard.
*/
