/* book Worked example 2: Q: An airliner of weight W = 500 kN pulls up at n = 2.5. The wing lift acts a = 0.5 m behind the CG, the wing pitching moment is M₀ = 150 kN·m nose-down, and the tailplane load acts lt = 15 m behind the CG. (a) Find the tail load and the wing lift. (b) The tail unit has a mass of 800 kg at the tail load line. Find the bending moment at a frame 10 m forward of the tail, and the bending stress there for a stiffened tube of mean radius 1.2 m with an equivalent thickness of 3.0 mm. Take g = 9.81 m/s².
   1. P = −(n W a + M₀) ÷ (lt − a) = −(2.5 × 500 × 0.5 + 150) ÷ 14.5 = −775 ÷ 14.5 = −53.45 kN, a download.
   2. Lw = n W − P = 1250 + 53.45 = 1303.45 kN. Check about the CG: −1303.45 × 0.5 − 150 + 53.45 × 15 = −651.7 − 150 + 801.7 = 0.
   3. Tail inertia: n m g = 2.5 × 800 × 9.81 = 19.62 kN downward, so the load aft of the frame is 53.45 + 19.62 = 73.07 kN.
   4. Moment at the frame: M = 73.07 × 10 = 730.7 kN·m, top of the fuselage in tension.
   5. I = π × 1.2³ × 0.003 = 0.01629 m⁴; σb = 730 700 × 1.2 ÷ 0.01629 = 53.8 MPa.
   Answer: P = −53.45 kN (download) and Lw = 1303.45 kN. At the frame M = 730.7 kN·m, giving ±53.8 MPa (top in tension). A full check also adds the inertia of the rear-fuselage structure and payload aft of the frame. */
